This is equivalent to the original, so expect only noise-level gains at best. The copy constructor already does the minimum: it allocates and copies both vectors.

The rewrite builds the two members from iterator ranges instead of calling their copy constructors. With random-access iterators, the library computes the size once and makes one allocation per vector. The element-wise copy of `values` stays the same, so every value, size and side effect matches the original.

```cpp
FieldBase::FieldBase(const FieldBase &field)
    : values(field.values.begin(), field.values.end()),
      stringIndexes(field.stringIndexes.begin(), field.stringIndexes.end())
{
}
```